{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"SUSE-SU-2025:03650-1","published":"2025-10-18T10:04:27Z","modified":"2026-03-23T04:50:00.231851Z","related":["CVE-2025-38110","CVE-2025-38206","CVE-2025-38396","CVE-2025-38471","CVE-2025-38499","CVE-2025-38566","CVE-2025-38644","CVE-2025-38678"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-38110","CVE-2025-38206","CVE-2025-38396","CVE-2025-38471","CVE-2025-38499","CVE-2025-38566","CVE-2025-38644","CVE-2025-38678"],"summary":"Security update for the Linux Kernel RT (Live Patch 0 for SLE 15 SP7)","details":"This update for the Linux Kernel 6.4.0-150700_5 fixes several issues.\n\nThe following security issues were fixed:\n\n- CVE-2025-38678: netfilter: nf_tables: reject duplicate device on updates (bsc#1249534).\n- CVE-2025-38499: clone_private_mnt(): make sure that caller has CAP_SYS_ADMIN in the right userns (bsc#1248673).\n- CVE-2025-38396: fs: export anon_inode_make_secure_inode() and fix secretmem LSM bypass (bsc#1247158).\n- CVE-2025-38566: sunrpc: fix handling of server side tls alerts (bsc#1248376).\n- CVE-2025-38110: net/mdiobus: Fix potential out-of-bounds clause 45 read/write access (bsc#1249458).\n- CVE-2025-38644: wifi: mac80211: reject TDLS operations when station is not associated (bsc#1248749).\n- CVE-2025-38206: exfat: fix double free in delayed_free (bsc#1246075).\n- CVE-2025-38471: tls: always refresh the queue when reading sock (bsc#1247452).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel-livepatch-SLE15-SP6-RT_Update_10","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Live Patching 15 SP6","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kernel-livepatch-SLE15-SP6-RT_Update_10&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Live%20Patching%2015%20SP6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8-150600.2.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"kernel-livepatch-6_4_0-150600_10_34-rt":"8-150600.2.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2025:03650-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-livepatch-SLE15-SP7-RT_Update_0","ec